cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use HexaLoam in your research, coursework, or robot build, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "HexaLoam: Open-Source 3D-Printable Hexapod Robot Platform (SOLIDWORKS, MG996R, LiDAR, MATLAB)"
type: software
version: 1.0.2
date-released: 2026-11-27
authors:
  - name: "HexaLoam contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/equesai/HexaLoam"
url: "https://equesai.github.io/HexaLoam/"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  HexaLoam is an open-source, fully 3D-printable hexapod robot with native editable SOLIDWORKS CAD.
  It has 18 joints (3 per leg) driven by 36 MG996R servos, two back-to-back per joint, and a PLA+
  structure of 5 STL designs (20 printed pieces, 1.306 kg as sliced). The chassis CAD integrates an
  RP-Lidar (2D) mount and cover. The repository provides STEP, STL, 3MF and GLB files, MATLAB Simscape
  Multibody and URDF models, four controller configurations (Arduino Mega, ESP32, Raspberry Pi with one
  or two ESP32), wiring diagrams, firmware, a Raspberry Pi Python and ROS 2 controller, and a
  mass-versus-torque analysis per configuration and gait. The design was tested by simulation and
  analysis; physical tests are pending. It has no camera mount or plant-vision code yet; a guide
  describes how to add them for agricultural plant inspection.
keywords:
  - HexaLoam
  - hexapod
  - hexabot
  - agricultural robotics
  - plant inspection
  - SOLIDWORKS
  - MATLAB
  - Simscape
  - ROS 2
  - 3D printing
  - MG996R
  - LiDAR
  - legged robot
  - multibody simulation
